    "durationMs": 274696,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation** — NestJS 11 + TypeORM + PostgreSQL (`src/`):\n- `POST /links` — validates `url` (absolute http/https with host) and optional `code` (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`), returns `201 {\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the URL unchanged; auto-generates an 8-char code when omitted (with collision retry); duplicate custom code → `409 {\"error\"}` (pre-check + unique-constraint race safety)\n- `GET /links/{code}` → `200` or `404 {\"error\"}`; `GET /r/{code}` → `302` with `Location`, incrementing clicks via a single atomic `UPDATE`; `GET /links` → `{\"items\",\"total\"}` in ascending creation order\n- All input errors (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code) → `422 {\"error\"}` via a ValidationPipe + global exception filter that maps 400s to 422\n- Schema created by a TypeORM migration (no `synchronize`); credentials read only from `DATABASE_URL`; `start.sh` builds, applies pending migrations, and serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup\n\n**Verification** — I ran the full requirement matrix over HTTP: all status codes, error shapes, redirect Location headers, exact-once click increments, list ordering, and a restart cycle proving data and click counts survive (2 clicks before restart, incremented to 3 after). Three cold starts of `sh start.sh` worked, including from a pristine database.\n\nOne environment quirk worth noting: `NODE_ENV=production` here makes npm omit devDependencies, so the `@types/*` packages are installed as regular dependencies to keep the build working in any environment. The database is left pristine and no servers are left running."
  }
